finding: Pending commits are not tied to the draw that encoded their work. GlobalTransformHistory's callback (global-transform.ts:78-84) clears tickCount, staging ranges, historyDiscarded and discontinuities on every successful group merely because enabled is true, even when prepareGlobalTransformFrame did not run. Independent reproduction on HEAD in an isolated copy: extend the kept aborted-history test by removing BeginFrameSystem for one successful step(0), then re-add it and retry; previous x is 0 rather than 10. Thus a successful unrelated/empty frame consumes history whose commands were discarded, and the later frame cannot recover it. The cluster and shadow callbacks likewise accept pendingUsed/casterSelectionPending left by an aborted frame if their producer no longer runs (removed, paused, or replaced); they have no frame identity or abort invalidation. Point-caster selection is in simulation, so its callback also does not establish that the atlas work actually encoded. The kept tests cover only immediate retries with all producers still running. Reloaded unkeyed resources stack permanent callbacks committing stale runtimes. Clusters and clusterGpuKey have no key; shadowRuntimeKey has no key either. Each newly created declaration appends a closure to World._frameSubmitCallbacks, with no deregistration or replacement until disposal. Independently importing cluster.ts under a fresh module identity yields a distinct Clusters value; after setting the old runtime's pending value to 123, an empty successful frame commits old.last from 0 to 123 even though only the fresh declaration is active. Real reload after an abort leaves exactly such pending old state. Repeated reloads retain and traverse all old runtime closures, contradicting the intended single current-resource commit path. GlobalTransformHistory does have a stable key and avoids this specific issue. Focused HEAD files pass (32 tests), and both kept regressions demonstrably fail with their source fixes reverted in an isolated copy: GlobalTransform expected previous x=10, received 0; point-shadow expected incumbent eid 2, received challenger eid 3. Worktree code was not edited.
